{
  "note": "Bank holidays 1974-1999 for the UK: the days appointed each year by Royal Proclamation (and, for Northern Ireland, by Order of the Secretary of State) as published in The Gazette, transcribed from docs/sources/uk-bank-holidays-1974-1999.md. Compiled 2026-10-25 for bizdays-toolkit 0.21.0. No government web list exists for these years; Hansard written answers (1976-1995) are the second source where found and never differ in dates.",
  "principle": "Schedule 1 of the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 gives the recurring days; every other day the providers return for 1974-1999 must appear here as a proclaimed or ordered day, or be listed in unverified. Days the law moves on its own (a Sunday holiday moved by Schedule 1) are not proclaimed and not listed.",
  "fieldNotes": {
    "mode": "'added' = appointed under section 1(3); 'in-place-of YYYY-MM-DD' = appointed under section 1(2) in place of that day",
    "source": "The Gazette edition, issue and page (or notice ID) and the publication date; 'notice only' = only the Privy Council Office notice was found, not the proclamation text",
    "unverified": "days the providers return by rule for which no proclamation or Order was found (gaps in The Gazette's online holdings: London Gazette issues 50761-50763 and 50779-50790 (30 Dec 1986 - 2 Jan 1987) and Belfast Gazette issues 4660-5171 (27 Dec 1985 - 4 Jan 1991) are listed by The Gazette as missing online); kept because the annual practice is unbroken. dateCertainty 'fixed' = the date itself leaves no choice; 'substitute-inferred' = the day is a substitute whose direction is inferred from the Orders of other years (see inferredFrom)",
    "unproclaimed": "Saturday holidays in Scotland for which no appointment was found; none in 1974-1999 (Appendix B of the record)",
    "easterSunday": "Easter Sunday 1974-1999 from a source independent of the library, used by the test to compute the Schedule 1 days",
    "weekends": "Holidays falling on a Saturday or Sunday are not listed by the providers (the convention of GOV.UK's lists), even where Schedule 1 keeps the Saturday as a bank holiday (26 December) or a proclamation appointed an additional day without disapplying the Saturday; see decisions.md 49"
  },
  "easterSunday": {
    "source": "U.S. Naval Observatory, Selected Christian Observances (https://aa.usno.navy.mil/data/christian_observances), one page per year; identical to the U.S. Census Bureau table 'Easter Dates from 1600 to 2099' (https://www.census.gov/data/software/x13as/genhol/easter-dates.html) and to the NOAA/NWS Peoria list for 1974-1999. Hansard 1976-07-12 and 1992-10-26 give Good Friday / Easter Monday of 1977 and 1992, which agree.",
